RolyPoly is an RNA virus analysis toolkit, meant to be a "swiss-army knife" for RNA virus discovery and characterization. It brings together commands, wrappers, parsers and automations covering a virus investigation from raw read processing to genome annotation, including an end-to-end pipeline.

It has two aims: to let non-computational researchers take a deep dive into their own data using tools that are friendly to non-specialists, and to let developers of virus analysis pipelines plug gaps in their own frameworks with individual RolyPoly commands.

RolyPoly is open source and still under active development, installable from PyPI (`rolypoly-tk`) and Bioconda.
